# Monstrous Emergence: "choose a creature you control" (CR 701.4a): Bot1 chooses its Elvish Mystic (1/1) on the battlefield - only chosen, nothing is revealed and the
# Mystic stays - and the spell deals damage equal to its power, 1, to Bot2's Grizzly Bears (2/2), which survives with 1 damage. The amount is the beheld creature's power, not
# the target's or a fixed number. The Bears is Bot2's creature, which is not one Bot1 controls, so it is not offered to be chosen.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Emerald
Mox Jet
Elvish Mystic
Monstrous Emergence
Forest x3
Forest x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Emerald
Mox Ruby
Grizzly Bears
Mountain x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Elvish Mystic.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Grizzly Bears.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Monstrous Emergence.Cast(Target: Grizzly Bears)
! Bot1.Choose(Grizzly Bears)
Bot1.Choose(Elvish Mystic)
? Bot1.Revealed = (absent)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot2.Battlefield.Grizzly Bears.Damage = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Elvish Mystic.Damage = 0
Bot1.Graveyard = Monstrous Emergence
